# Story: someone pins a call in the top right corner and lets the editor fill the screen. On a Mac the call used to lie
# wholly behind the editor, while the menu's tick said "kept in view": macOS lets nobody lift another app's window over
# the one that has the keyboard. Now the call has room of its own beside every view, as the Dock has, and nothing is raised.
# Reference: F49, collab/QUESTIONS.md Q25, board 1.25. Window ids start at 101. The display is 1440x900, visible 0,25 1440x875.
mac-tiling off
open Editor
open Browser
open Zoom 320x240
move 103 1090 50 320 240
pin 103
expect replied keeping w103 in view
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
expect clear 103
# The editor has the keyboard and fills the screen: all that is left of it. The call is behind it in macOS's order, and all of it shows.
focus 101
zoom
expect fills 101
expect clear 103
expect in-front 103
expect covered 103 no
expect at 103 1090 50
expect focused 101
# Every other view too: the neighbour, the Desktop, everything.
neighbor right
expect clear 103
neighbor right
expect fills 102
expect clear 103
show-all
expect clear 103
expect at 103 1090 50
# Clicking about raises nothing and covers nothing.
focus 102
focus 101
expect in-front 103
# Dragged to the other side: the docked windows wait until it is let go, and then move once.
pick-up 103 700 400
expect still 101
expect still 102
let-go
drag 103 180 70
expect moved-once
expect clear 103
expect left-of 103 101
expect pinned 103
# In the middle there is no room to make: more than four tenths of the screen would go. It stays in view, and Arbor says what is so.
drag 103 720 340
expect said Zoom stays in view, but other windows can cover it here
zoom 101
expect fills 101
expect visible 103
expect covered 103 yes
show-all
# Back at an edge it has its room again.
drag 103 1250 60
expect clear 103
zoom 101
expect clear 103
expect covered 103 no
show-all
# In the Dock its room goes back to the others, and comes again with it: there and back is nothing.
minimize 103
flush
zoom 101
expect fills 101
show-all
restore 103
flush
expect clear 103
# Its own app makes it larger, in steps, as when somebody shares a screen: the others follow once it stands still.
move 103 1060 50 350 260
move 103 1030 50 380 280
move 103 1000 50 410 300
expect still 101
wait 0.4
expect moved-once
expect clear 103
# Taking the pin off gives the room back.
unpin 103
expect ok
zoom 101
expect fills 101
expect hidden 103
